From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: expose ABGR2101010 and XBGR2101010 on planes

The format table already describes both layouts, linear and UBWC, and
the hardware scans them out, but the plane format lists and the UBWC
list only offered the ARGB/XRGB orders. A2B10G10R10 is the 10-bit
swapchain format of Vulkan HDR10 games, so such a buffer could not be
scanned out and the compositor had to copy it.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_catalog.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_catalog.c
index 08b0c63dc..01de4dd8e 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_catalog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_hw_catalog.c
@@ -121,6 +121,8 @@ static const uint32_t plane_formats[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010,
 	DRM_FORMAT_XRGB2101010,
+	DRM_FORMAT_ABGR2101010,
+	DRM_FORMAT_XBGR2101010,
 	DRM_FORMAT_RGB888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_BGR888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_RGB565,
@@ -151,6 +153,8 @@ static const uint32_t plane_formats_yuv[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_BGRA8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010,
 	DRM_FORMAT_XRGB2101010,
+	DRM_FORMAT_ABGR2101010,
+	DRM_FORMAT_XBGR2101010,
 	DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_XBGR8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_RGBX8888,
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
index e1f7d4ce0..9a538bc98 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_plane.c
@@ -74,6 +74,8 @@ static const uint32_t qcom_compressed_supported_formats[] = {
 	DRM_FORMAT_XRGB8888,
 	DRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010,
 	DRM_FORMAT_XRGB2101010,
+	DRM_FORMAT_ABGR2101010,
+	DRM_FORMAT_XBGR2101010,
 	DRM_FORMAT_BGR565,
 
 	DRM_FORMAT_NV12,
